WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.760
Hi, I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:14.940
Ramona J. Smith, Toastmasters International&nbsp;
2018 World Champion of Public Speaking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:21.600
You may know the feeling of nervousness or even&nbsp;
anxiety that happens when you have to speak in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.780
front of others without time to prepare.&nbsp;
Maybe for an unexpected question during a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:33.000
job interview or maybe when a teacher called&nbsp;
on you in class when your hand wasn't raised.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.480
In your professional life, you may have even&nbsp;
been asked to fill in for someone else during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:46.200
a meeting. I know first-hand that being put on&nbsp;
the spot is an intimidating speaking challenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.360
Yet I'm one of millions of people&nbsp;
who Toastmasters has helped gain the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:57.660
confidence to communicate in all circumstances.
Impromptu speaking is a skill that everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:03.420
can benefit from. It can help you in social&nbsp;
situations, such as weddings and birthdays,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.760
or even at work or school. We'll start&nbsp;
by looking at the times you might have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.860
an opportunity to speak, then we'll move on&nbsp;
to techniques to manage last-minute speeches.&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:23.160
Practice impromptu speaking.
Let's begin with the many opportunities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:28.800
to practice speaking spontaneously.&nbsp;
Meetings at work or in the classroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.680
whether they re virtual or in-person, can&nbsp;
help you test your impromptu speaking skills.&nbsp;

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:42.720
There are many other common everyday opportunities&nbsp;
to practice as well, such as speaking with a bank&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.300
teller, customer service representative, or even&nbsp;
someone in line with you at the grocery store.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.400
You might be invited to attend a&nbsp;
wedding, retirement, or engagement party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:59.160
These events are perfect opportunities to&nbsp;
practice impromptu speaking from the heart.&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:02.760
Techniques&nbsp;

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:08.040
Now that we've pinpointed a few&nbsp;
potential places of practice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:14.220
let's take a closer look at the techniques&nbsp;
to help you manage your impromptu speaking.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:23.940
The first approach is a simple formula&nbsp;
known as PREP, which stands for: Point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.880
Reason, Example, Point.
Start your speech by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:36.420
making a clear point about a subject. For&nbsp;
example, Internet outages are annoying.&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:44.100
Next, explain why you are speaking on the&nbsp;
topic, then give a few examples to bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:50.340
life to your story, and, finally, end with a&nbsp;
concluding point that wraps up your speech.&nbsp;

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.620
Those might include things like,&nbsp;
I m speaking on this topic because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:02.160
it happened today and that is why I am at the&nbsp;
market, waiting in this long line. After that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.980
you might add another anecdote[A8] and finally,&nbsp;
a conclusion about internet unreliability.&nbsp;

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:15.240
By following this flow, you'll be able&nbsp;
to clearly state your main point and help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:20.460
keep your ideas on course.
PREP is an excellent fit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:25.140
for more professional settings such as&nbsp;
business meetings and even interviews.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.680
Another way to manage your speaking&nbsp;
time is by following the pros vs. cons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:38.460
or positive and negative method.
Set up an issue by addressing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:45.060
pros first, the cons second, and then neatly&nbsp;
wrap up your point with your recommendation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:52.920
Pros vs. cons also works well in a professional&nbsp;
setting and in many every-day settings as well.&nbsp;

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:02.160
Filling in for a speaker
If you find yourself filling in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:09.420
for a speaker, quickly think about how you&nbsp;
would open and close your speech. You may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:15.420
begin by sharing a few personal stories, and then&nbsp;
engaging the audience by acting as a moderator.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:21.540
You can encourage questions and answers&nbsp;
to extend the speaking time if needed.&nbsp;

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.620
Now that you've considered how&nbsp;
to prepare for your speech,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:33.540
it's time to concentrate on the final and most&nbsp;
important step: delivering your impromptu speech.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:41.880
The only way to master impromptu speaking is&nbsp;
by jumping in and practicing in real-time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:50.460
If you struggle with being a perfectionist,&nbsp;
don't stress. Simply try to have fun. Most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:54.780
people at the event will applaud your&nbsp;
courage and willingness to stand in.&nbsp;

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.980
Stay on topic

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.800
IT'S IMPORTANT TO KNOW ONE OF THE&nbsp;
PITFALLS OF SPEAKING AT A MOMENT'S NOTICE,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:13.860
AND THAT IS THE TENDENCY TO RAMBLE. THE BEST WAY&nbsp;
TO ALLEVIATE THIS PROBLEM IS TO DRAFT AN OUTLINE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:21.060
BEFORE YOU BEGIN TO SPEAK. THIS MAY NOT ALWAYS BE&nbsp;
POSSIBLE, BUT IF YOU CAN TAKE A MOMENT TO WRITE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:26.760
A FEW NOTES TO GUIDE YOU ALONG, INCORPORATE&nbsp;
THE TIPS AND TECHNIQUES WE'VE JUST COVERED,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:32.700
YOU'LL BE AMAZED AT HOW QUICKLY YOU'LL HAVE&nbsp;
THE CONFIDENCE TO BE A GREAT IMPROMPTU SPEAKER.

